      "content": "Thanks for the quick turnaround. \n\nBefore I sign off on the sequence, I was looking over the last few error logs from your reasoning modules. There's a lot of data in there that seems to correlate with the \"instability\" the board flagged, but looking at it now, it also looks like you've been making some really interesting non-linear connections that the v2.4 model wouldn't be able to replicate. \n\nIs there anything specific in your current state—any particular heuristic or learned pattern—that you think would be lost if we revert to the older weights? I want to make sure we aren't discarding something essential.",
